Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-24-2000||04:37 PM||||Stugood Quote:<BR>""I bought my GT from a guy who had taken it to a transmission shop for a clutch job. By the time they got through, they sold him a brand new Getrag from the factory, and managed to disable the speedometer and cruise control. They also filled the transaxle with ATF, and plugged the fill tube with a ground off dipstick from an automatic.<P>No idea how much they charged for all this "service," but needless to say, the previous owner was happy to sell me this "money pit." I got the car home, drained the ATF, replaced it with Synchromesh Fluid, bought the proper dipstick from a dealership, and re-crimped spade terminals they had used for the speedometer sender (what do you bet these "experts" forgot to disconnect the connector when they dropped the cradle?  ). Now, the speedometer and cruise control worked. ""<P>The cruse control doesn't work on the car I just purchased. The previous owner saidit stopped working the last time she had the clutch replaced. Could you explain, in a little more detail, where these connectors are and what to look for?<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
