Z||000005||AL||07-24-2000||07:56 PM||||they are two wires that is connected to a connector which is white and is under the dash, take the bottom part off and you will see it,when you disconect it, the two wires will have a connector that looks like a fork,what you have to do is replace the arm for thecruise control mine didn't work until i changed that arm, but first check your hoses and jar in the back to see if you don't have a leak,disconnect one of the small hoses and blow in it if you don't here a hiss then you know it's the arm, good luck,AL.<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||trigger||07-24-2000||08:18 PM||||Hi,<P>One way to check the arm is to look at the clear spade connector mentioned before.  Look at the four little wires soddered to the connector.  If the sodder is good odds are that the arm is good.  Although mine got cut at the top when the washer arm got broke by the previous owner.  I just got a new arm yesterday and love it.||||reg||1
